    "result_text": "Done. Full suite green: **38 tests, 0 failures**.\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe spec adds a read-time derived field `contactPreference` to the owner response. Following the existing pattern for other derived fields (`membershipLevel`, `locality` \u2014 `@Transient` getters on `Owner`, declared as `readOnly` in `openapi.yml`, mapped by name via MapStruct), I made two changes:\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `@Transient getContactPreference()` returning `\"EMAIL\"` when an email is present (non-null, non-blank), otherwise `\"PHONE\"`.\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `contactPreference` property (`readOnly` string) to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gets the field and MapStruct auto-maps it by name.\n\nNo mapper or YAML pipeline changes were needed \u2014 the getter flows straight through the existing `RespondWithOwner` \u2192 `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto` path used by `GET /api/owners/{id}`. Both new tests (`corePhoneWhenNoEmail`, `functionalityEmailWhenPresent`) pass.",
